  "stem": {
   "en": "The pole pieces of a moving coil galvanometer are made concave to produce a radial field. This is done so that:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "the spring does not break"
   },
   {
    "en": "the torque is the same at every position of the coil and the scale is linear"
   },
   {
    "en": "the field becomes zero at the coil"
   },
   {
    "en": "the coil does not heat up"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "In a radial field the coil's plane is always parallel to B, so τ = NIAB and φ ∝ I."
  },
